\section*{Multiplication}

4MHMA05

\section*{5.1 Multiplying by Tens}

Ajay packs 10 laddoos in one box. How many laddoos are there in 23 boxes?

We write: \(23 \times 10=230\).

When we multiply a number by 10 , we write a zero after the number.

Example 1: \(45 \times 10=450\)

Example 2: A shop sells 20 pencils in one packet. How many pencils are
there in 14 packets?

\[
14 \times 20=14 \times 2 \times 10=280
\]

There are 280 pencils in 14 packets.

\section*{5.2 Multiplying Two-digit Numbers}

To multiply \(34 \times 12\), we split 12 into 10 and 2 .

\[
34 \times 12=34 \times 10+34 \times 2=340+68=408
\]

Example 3: A row has 26 chairs. The hall has 15 rows. How many chairs are
there in the hall?

\[
26 \times 15=26 \times 10+26 \times 5=260+130=390
\]

